; xfail: expected '}'
;
; A syntax error INSIDE a class/union/trait body must HARD-FAIL the compile
; with the real inner error, not be silently swallowed. parse_class/parse_union/
; parse_trait treat the Body as an optional field; the old codegen discarded a
; committed Invalid from parse_body (`when i: Invalid {}`), leaving the lexer
; parked mid-body so the class parsed as if it had no body and the garbage was
; silently dropped (compile succeeded, rc 0) — or re-surfaced as a bogus outer
; "expected '}'". The generator now propagates an Invalid from any optional
; field whose opener is unambiguous (here the body's `{`), so the "expected '}'"
; from parse_body reaches the user.
;
; Self-hosted-only: the frozen C++ stage-0 llvm::consumeError's the same site.

define Foo()
{
    function good() returns int
    {
        return 1
    }
    @#$ garbage that is not a member
}
